## Upstream provenance

The debate engine in this repository is derived from the project
**dsh-ai-debate** (https://github.com/alicia1030su/dsh-ai-debate),
Copyright (C) 2026 the dsh-ai-debate authors, also licensed AGPL-3.0-only.

What was taken from upstream: the discussion import/parsing pipeline, the
comment-chain and target resolution logic, stance analysis and dispute
summarisation, persona and argument strategies, model invocation and result
handling, candidate generation/edit/re-evaluation, the safety checks and
prompt-injection defences, the manual approval and copy flow, the platform
adapters and capability diagnostics, and the configuration/persistence/logging
model.

What was replaced: the host integration. Upstream ran as a plugin inside DSH
(a Cordis-based AI host) and relied on its settings service, credential store,
web server, plugin lifecycle, browser module loader and login session. This
repository ships a standalone runtime for those responsibilities — its own
configuration file, encrypted credential store, administrator authentication,
HTTP server, background job queue and web console — so that the program runs
without DSH, Node.js, Docker or Python installed.

The upstream repository, its tags, releases, documentation and user data are
unchanged and remain the canonical history of the plugin. This repository is a
separate, independent product; the mention of the upstream project here is
attribution, not a runtime dependency.

